{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$g(x)$ is the quotient of two, more basic, expressions: $\\sin(x)$ and $\\sqrt{x}$.\n\nTherefore, the derivative of $g$ can be found using **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}g'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{\\sin(x)}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x))\\sqrt{x}-\\sin(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\sqrt{x})}{(\\sqrt{x})^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{\\cos(x)\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-\\sin(x)\\cdot \\dfrac1{2\\sqrt{x}}}{(\\sqrt{x})^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }\\sin(x)\\text{ and }\\sqrt{x}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x}\\cos(x)-\\dfrac{\\sin(x)}{2\\sqrt{x}}}{x}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{2x\\cos(x)-\\sin(x)}{2x\\sqrt{x}}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$g'(x)=\\dfrac{2x\\cos(x)-\\sin(x)}{2x\\sqrt{x}}$\n\nor any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=\\dfrac{\\sin(x)}{\\sqrt{x}}$.\n\n$g'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]\n","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{2x\\cos\\left(x\\right)-\\sin\\left(x\\right)}{2x\\sqrt{x}}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
